# 18. Notebook vs Python Script

A major objective of this project is understanding when notebooks and scripts should be used.

## 18.1 Jupyter Notebook

Notebooks are well suited for:

* Exploratory data analysis.
* Interactive experimentation.
* Visualization.
* Testing hypotheses.
* Iterative investigation.
* Communicating analytical findings.

A notebook allows developers and analysts to execute code incrementally and immediately inspect results.

## 18.2 Python Script

Python scripts are better suited for:

* Repeatable workflows.
* Automated data processing.
* Command-line execution.
* Scheduled jobs.
* CI/CD systems.
* Reusable business logic.
* Production pipelines.
* Team-maintained code.

A production workflow should not depend on a developer manually executing notebook cells in the correct order.

